  "question": {
    "text": "<p>The radius <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mi>r</mi></mfenced></math>, length <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mi>l</mi></mfenced></math> and resistance <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mi>R</mi></mfenced></math> of a metal wire was measured in the laboratory as</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>.35</mo><mo>±</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.05</mo></mrow></mfenced><mo> </mo><mi>cm</mi></math>, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>100</mn><mo>±</mo><mn>10</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo> </mo><mi>ohm</mi></math>, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>l</mi><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>15</mn><mo>±</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.2</mo></mrow></mfenced><mo> </mo><mi>cm</mi></math></p><p>The percentage error in resistivity of the material of the wire is :</p>",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
